Copyright (c) 2026 Zain Dana Harper. All rights reserved.

This repository is the source of harperz9.github.io. Three sets of terms apply
to it.

1. Written works are licensed under CC BY 4.0. LICENSE-TEXT lists the papers,
   essays, briefings and reading pages it covers, and it governs them.

2. Third-party and vendored code, fonts and other material keep the licence
   of their source. The table below lists each one, and a licence file or
   note sits beside it in the repository.

3. Everything else is all rights reserved. That covers the site's own code
   (HTML, CSS, JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, build scripts, tools and
   tests), its design and layout, the art, figures, generated imagery and
   media made for the site, the brand and the author's own typefaces, and
   the biography, career and portfolio pages.

Under the third set of terms you may view the site and this repository, and
fork the repository on GitHub as GitHub's Terms of Service allow. You may read
the code to learn from it, to review it, or to build software that works with
the site. You may quote short excerpts with credit. Copying, modifying,
redistributing or building derivative works from this material needs written
permission from the author (github.com/HarperZ9).

The reusable engines behind the site live in their own repositories. Each of
those repositories carries its own licence, and that licence governs it.

## Third-party and vendored material

| Path | What it is | Licence |
|---|---|---|
| `system/lib/vendor/d3-7.9.0.*` | D3 7.9.0, Mike Bostock | ISC, see the `.LICENSE.txt` beside it |
| `system/lib/vendor/panzoom-anvaka-9.4.3.*` | panzoom 9.4.3, Andrei Kashcha | MIT, see the `.LICENSE.txt` beside it |
| `system/lib/vendor/tweakpane-4.0.5.*` | Tweakpane 4.0.5, cocopon | MIT, see the `.LICENSE.txt` beside it |
| `system/lib/reconcile/` | reconcile, by the author, synced from its repository | the `LICENSE` in that directory; see `LICENSE-NOTE.md` there |
| `system/vendor/learn/` | Learn, by the author, pinned by `VENDOR.json` | the `LICENSE` in that directory |
| `system/media-engine/contracts.mjs`, `tests/superstack/` | superstack v0.1.0, by the author | MIT, see the header of `contracts.mjs` and `tests/superstack/README.md` |
| `media/raw-native/wasm-0.4.0/` | raw-native v0.4.0 build, by the author | FSL-1.1-MIT, see `LICENSE-NOTE.md` there |
| `plugins/data/*/LICENSE` | copies of each plugin's licence, shown on its terms page | each plugin's own licence |
| `assets/*.js` | compiled home page, which bundles React, react-dom and scheduler | MIT, see `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md` |
| `system/fonts/hanken-grotesk*` | Hanken Grotesk, The Hanken Grotesk Project Authors | SIL Open Font License 1.1, see `system/fonts/OFL-hanken-grotesk.txt` |
| `system/fonts/conso-*` | Conso, Pavel Larin | the designer's terms, see `system/fonts/FONTS.md` |
| `system/fonts/kilon*`, `system/fonts/telos-display*` | Kilon, Ahmad Suhadi (suhadidesign), and Telos Display, built from it | the designer's terms, see `system/fonts/FONTS.md` |

Quoted material from other authors, and images or figures credited to others,
stay under their owners' terms.
